commit 3b80c8d3d4e2656d1190fa99ef6bd48775783709 (HEAD -> logind-improvements/21)
Author: John Soo <jsoo1@asu.edu>
Date:   Wed Feb 12 16:12:28 2025 -0700

    systemd-logind: TakeControl of existing session on vtno
    
    Otherwise, fall back to session for PID.
    
    This allows a daemonized X to be spawned by a process that is not
    owned by the desired vtno.
    
    This is to address the rootless X with a user service scenario. In
    that case X will be spawned by an init process as the user. So the tty
    associated to getpid() will not match the desired one specified in vtno.
    
    When that happens, even if the user owns the desired vt, logind won't
    be able to take over the session.

diff --git a/hw/xfree86/os-support/linux/systemd-logind.c b/hw/xfree86/os-support/linux/systemd-logind.c
